<title>FRANCE: Havas offers CEP minorities 470 Ffr/share.</title>
<headline>Havas offers CEP minorities 470 Ffr/share.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French media group Havas said on Thursday it was offering to buy out CEP Communication minority shareholders at 470 francs per share, making the total worth 2.7 billion francs.</p>
<p>CEP shares were suspended on Wednesday at 400 francs.</p>
<p>Havas already owns 74.2 percent of CEP, a French specialist publishing house.</p>
<p>The statement was released after board meetings at Havas and CEP on Thursday afternoon.</p>
</text>
